      "elapsed_sec": 20.58,
      "word_count": 192,
      "answer": "For your flight from San Francisco to London with 12 passengers, the Gulfstream G650 is an excellent choice. This aircraft is well-suited for long-range travel, providing the necessary comfort and performance for such a mission.\n\nThe Gulfstream G650 has a range of approximately 7,000 nautical miles, allowing for a nonstop flight between these two cities without the need for refueling. It can accommodate up to 16 passengers, making it ideal for your group size. \n\n- Gulfstream G650\n - Range: ~7,000 nautical miles\n - Passengers: Up to 16\n - Typical acquisition band: ≈ $45,000,000\n - Reason it fits: Designed for nonstop flights between major global city pairs, ensuring a comfortable and efficient travel experience.\n\nAs an alternative, you might also consider the Bombardier Global 7500, which offers slightly more range and passenger capacity:\n\n- Global 7500\n - Range: ~7,700 nautical miles\n - Passengers: Up to 17\n - Typical acquisition band: ≈ $52,000,000\n - Reason it fits: Capable of the longest nonstop missions, perfect for larger delegations.\n\nBoth aircraft provide excellent comfort and functionality for your travel requirements. If you need further details on specifications or wish to explore other models, feel free to ask! \n\n✅ GOOD FIT",
