      "elapsed_sec": 24.7,
      "word_count": 188,
      "answer": "The Gulfstream G700 and Bombardier Global 7500 are both exceptional ultra-long-range jets, each with unique strengths. Here’s a concise comparison to help you evaluate them based on your mission needs:\n\nRange\n- G700: 7,750 nautical miles\n- Global 7500: 7,700 nautical miles\n\nPassengers\n- G700: Accommodates up to 19 passengers with customizable seating and up to five living areas.\n- Global 7500: Also seats up to 19 passengers, featuring a spacious four-zone cabin layout, including a dedicated master suite.\n\nCruise Speed\n- G700: Mach 0.935\n- Global 7500: Mach 0.925\n\nCabin Characteristics\n- G700: Offers a longer cabin at 56 ft 11 in, designed for multiple living zones that enhance space and comfort.\n- Global 7500: Known for its innovative design, including patented Nuage seating for long-haul comfort.\n\nOperational Economics\n- G700: Slightly lower operational costs and higher cruise speed.\n- Global 7500: Renowned for its comfort during long flights, making it a favorite for extended missions.\n\nIf your priority is passenger comfort and innovative cabin design, the Global 7500 may be the better choice. However, if you value range and operational efficiency, the G700 stands out. \n\n✅ GOOD FIT",
